{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Eleven days.</b> The reason he spoke these words during those eleven days <b>from Horeb.</b> For they journeyed from Horeb to Kadesh Barnea, and I have already told you that from Kadesh Barnea the spies went, and after HaShem swore that they would not enter the land, no commandments were renewed until the fortieth year, for so we find, and the proof is that he said \"he expounded this Torah\" — behold, he expounded the Torah that he spoke between Paran and between Tophel, for most of the commandments are in this book. And likewise he explained \"according to all that YHWH commanded him to them across the Jordan in the wilderness in the Arabah.\" And if you understand the sod of the years [twelve], also \"and Moses wrote\" and \"the Canaanite was then in the land\" and \"on the mountain of YHWH it will be seen\" and \"behold, his bed was a bed of iron,\" you will recognize the truth."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The reading השרים in parentheses is corrected to השנים [the years] per the marginal note צ״ל. The string of verse citations (Genesis 12:6, Genesis 22:14, Deuteronomy 3:11) is presented as Ibn Ezra gives them, with no connective tissue; each is a separate prooftext for the same principle. 'The years [twelve]' renders השנים, preserving the cryptic sod hint."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:50.309397192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}